---
import { isPublicPublication } from '../lib/publication/scope';
import { claimById, claimUrl, formatValue, figureById } from '../lib/evidence';
import { trendFoldRows, trendSupplementHash, ratePercent, variantContext } from '../lib/publication/supplement';
import { studyById } from '../lib/publication';
const study = studyById.get('trend-quality')!;
const publicRows = figureById.get('trend-folds')!.table.rows.filter(row => row.label.includes('V5'));
---
{isPublicPublication ? <section class="evidence-note fold-context" id="trend-fold-decision-context"><h4>Complete periods and the evidence boundary</h4><p>The archived table preserves Sharpe, completeness and the recorded period decisions. The additional return inputs and dates from a locally authorized supplement are omitted from the public edition. A positive Sharpe alone does not establish that all conditions passed; an overall false flag does not identify which individual condition failed.</p><dl>{publicRows.map(row => <div id={`fold-${row.label.split(' —')[0]}`} data-fold-context={row.label.split(' —')[0]} tabindex="-1"><dt>{row.label}</dt><dd>Archived Sharpe: {formatValue(row.value)}. {row.complete === false ? 'Partial period; descriptive only.' : 'Complete period.'} Archived overall decision: {String(row.conjunctive_fold_pass)}. The underlying return inputs are not included in the public edition; no individual return-condition result is inferred.</dd></div>)}</dl></section> : <section class="evidence-note fold-context" id="trend-fold-decision-context" aria-labelledby="fold-context-title" data-supplement-id="trend-fold-context-v1">
  <h4 id="fold-context-title">Why wf2 fails while wf4 passes</h4>
  <p>{study.researchObject} {study.question}</p>
  <p>{variantContext}</p>
  <p>A complete candidate period passes only if its net annual compound growth exceeds unfiltered S0, its growth after matching the unfiltered EMA comparator’s volatility exceeds EMA’s net growth, <strong>and</strong> its Sharpe is positive. All three are required. The return comparisons explain why positive Sharpe alone cannot decide either row.</p>
  <p>Earlier training events set each period’s quality threshold. The threshold then stays fixed in the later test. The dated intervals below are the configured calendar bounds, not a claim that every boundary was an exchange session. The partial final interval ends before another complete test period has elapsed and is excluded from the complete-period gate.</p>
  <p>For the EMA comparison, the recorded calculation scales candidate daily returns down when their volatility is higher than EMA’s. It never scales them up when the candidate already has lower volatility. The growth below is the saved result of that risk cap, rather than a new calculation from rounded annual growth.</p>
  <p class="small">The fold context supplement supplies the return comparisons and dates omitted by the original derivative. The archived flags, original table and figure remain unchanged. These checks compare saved inputs with the recorded rule; they do not rerun trading research.</p>
  <dl>{trendFoldRows.map(row=><div id={`fold-${row.period.id}`} data-fold-context={row.period.id}>
    <dt><strong>{row.period.id}</strong> · {row.period.complete ? 'Complete test period' : 'Partial period; excluded from the complete-period count'}</dt>
    <dd>Train <span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.train_start`}>{row.period.train_start}</span>–<span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.train_end`}>{row.period.train_end}</span>; test <span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.test_start`}>{row.period.test_start}</span>–<span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.test_end`}>{row.period.test_end}</span>.</dd>
    <dd><ol>
      <li>Net growth: <strong><span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.candidateNetCagr`}>{ratePercent(row.rates.candidateNetCagr)}</span></strong> versus S0 <strong><span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.s0NetCagr`}>{ratePercent(row.rates.s0NetCagr)}</span></strong> · {row.recordedConditionFlags[0]?'exceeds S0':'does not exceed S0'}.</li>
      <li>Growth with the EMA risk cap: <strong><span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.candidateVolMatchedCagr`}>{ratePercent(row.rates.candidateVolMatchedCagr)}</span></strong> versus EMA <strong><span data-supplement-key={`${row.period.id}.emaNetCagr`}>{ratePercent(row.rates.emaNetCagr)}</span></strong> · {row.recordedConditionFlags[1]?'exceeds EMA':'does not exceed EMA'}.</li>
      <li>Sharpe: <a href={claimUrl(row.existingSharpeClaimId)}>{formatValue(row.sharpe.value)}</a> · {row.recordedConditionFlags[2]?'positive':'not positive'}.</li>
    </ol></dd>
    <dd><strong>Archived flag:</strong> <a href={claimUrl(row.existingDecisionClaimId)}>{row.recordedOverallFlag?'true (passed)':'false'+(row.period.complete?' (failed)':' (descriptive only)')}</a>. {row.period.complete ? row.inspection.evaluation==='passed'?'All three conditions passed.':'At least one required condition failed; the individual comparisons above identify it.' : 'These observations remain descriptive; they cannot add a complete-period pass.'} <strong>Publication consistency:</strong> {row.period.complete?'agrees with the archived complete-period decision':'not evaluated for the complete-period gate'}.</dd>
    <dd><details><summary>Exact source precision and locators</summary><p>Annual return fractions, before percentage display: candidate net <code>{row.rates.candidateNetCagr}</code>; S0 net <code>{row.rates.s0NetCagr}</code>; candidate at EMA risk <code>{row.rates.candidateVolMatchedCagr}</code>; EMA net <code>{row.rates.emaNetCagr}</code>. Display multiplies by one hundred once; comparisons use unrounded source precision.</p><p><a href="/evidence/sources/#src-2adacd9e9309">Recorded walk-forward CSV</a>: V5 line {row.csvLocators.V5.line}, S0 line {row.csvLocators.S0.line}, EMA line {row.csvLocators.EMA.line}. Fields: <code>net_cagr</code> and <code>vol_matched_cagr_to_unfiltered_ema</code>. Dates: <a href="/evidence/sources/#src-c4562307c478">registered configuration</a>, <code>walk_forward.folds[{row.period.id}]</code>.</p></details></dd>
  </div>)}</dl>
  <p>The study required <a href={claimUrl('trend-complete-required')}>{formatValue(claimById.get('trend-complete-required')!.value)}</a> of <a href={claimUrl('trend-complete-folds')}>{formatValue(claimById.get('trend-complete-folds')!.value)}</a> complete periods; V5 recorded <a href={claimUrl('trend-v5-complete-passes')}>{formatValue(claimById.get('trend-v5-complete-passes')!.value)}</a>. Passing this count would still not replace the separate mechanism, concentration and familywise selection requirements. An absent gate field for the EMA comparator remains unavailable rather than becoming a failed candidate.</p>
  <p class="small">Supplement <code>trend-fold-context-v1</code> · SHA-256 <code>{trendSupplementHash}</code>. Public embedding and downloads remain unapproved.</p>
</section>}
